I stopped reading User Friendly several years ago when they went too far 
with an April Fool's joke so I have no idea if it's funny now, but it 
certainly used to be.

The thing to keep in mind is that all comic strips have a target 
audience. The majority of UF's audience, at least when I was reading it, 
was quite familiar with Nethack.

It's also my recollection that UF is best-read as a sequence. Individual 
strips may not be as good as a bunch in a row. If the strip referenced 
above is kicking off such a series, I wouldn't necessarily expect that 
it would be a laugh-riot on its own.

